  "interpretation": {
    "finding": "During the largest 2.521827 s gap between EGO successful takes, the upstream mapping_input_adapter recorded 50 camera-pose rmw_publish events; the largest gap between those writer events was 0.122401 s. The EGO RMW trace had no camera-pose taken=0 event, so it did not record failed take attempts for that reader; the long interval has no mapped take attempt between its endpoints. This rules out publisher silence at the RMW publish boundary as the explanation for this interval, but does not show whether Fast DDS delivered samples to the EGO DataReader or whether the executor wait set selected that subscription.",
    "navigation_outcome": "The run passed preconditions and dispatched the same 0.30 m/+30 degree goal, then aborted on the existing localization_accel_bias_norm_exceeded gate. PX4 entered AUTO_LAND, later briefly recorded DESCEND/failsafe, touched down and disarmed. ULog shows EV position/yaw/velocity fusion, zero GNSS aiding and zero dropout. These flight events are separate from the publisher/take timing result.",
    "root_cause": "UNRESOLVED between DDS DataReader delivery/readiness and ROS executor wait-set selection/scheduling. The generic executor tracepoints contain no selected-entity fields.",
    "limitations": [
      "RMW publish timestamps show calls at the writer boundary, not delivery or sample availability in the EGO reader.",
      "No message-header stamp was recorded at both ends, so individual published samples were not paired with EGO take records.",
      "This is one diagnostic run with a run-local EGO overlay. The action did not succeed because the existing accel-bias gate fired.",
      "The executor tracepoints provide activity counts but no subscription handle or ready-entity identity."
    ],
    "next_step": "Before another flight, inspect an isolated Fast DDS/RMW DataReader readiness or data-available observation for the EGO camera-pose reader. If it can be captured without changing QoS or adding high-bandwidth subscribers, run a bounded #229 comparison against EGO rmw_take and executor wait events."
  },
